  "articleBody": "Creating an accessible kitchen isn't just about meeting current needs; it's about designing a space that anticipates future mobility changes and provides comfort and usability for everyone. The key is thoughtful planning that focuses on movement and reach. Start by assessing the user’s specific needs—are we talking about wheelchair access, limited mobility, or just general ease of use? From there, we plan the 'work triangle' (sink, stove, refrigerator) and ensure ample clear floor space for easy maneuvering. A common mistake is creating a kitchen that looks accessible but still has tight turning spaces or awkward reach ranges. We pay close attention to details like counter heights, ensuring they accommodate both standing and seated users. Sink clearance with proper knee and toe space is crucial, as is the placement of appliances for easy access. We also consider pull-out storage solutions and lever-style hardware, which are much easier to operate than traditional knobs. Because accessible remodeling often involves demolition, cabinetry, plumbing, and electrical work all at once, precise coordination is essential. Small measurement errors can render a kitchen difficult or even impossible to use safely. If you're considering an accessible kitchen remodel in the Denver area, HH Remodeling LLC has the expertise to guide you through every step, ensuring a functional and beautiful outcome.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}